{"id": "lookup-mark-patterson", "question": "What does Mark Patterson research, and what is their title?", "stratum": "lookup", "kind": "prose", "ground_truth": "", "expected_slugs": ["mark-patterson"], "source_facts": "NAME: Mark Patterson TITLE: Professor, Chief Technology Officer, Global Resilience Institute Core Faculty Member, Coastal Sustainability Institute Affiliated Faculty Member, Institute for Experiential Robotics COLLEGE: cos SLUG: mark-patterson RESEARCH_INTERESTS: [\"Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (AUVs)\", \"Marine robotics\", \"Free-swimming marine robots\", \"Sensors and systems for ecophysiology\", \"Marine ecology and biomechanics\", \"Machine learning for underwater imagery\", \"Deep-sea autonomous vehicle swarms\", \"Biologically-inspired autonomy\", \"Microplastics detection\", \"Physical biology of invertebrates\", \"Physical biology of plants\", \"Physical biology of fishes\", \"Allometry of metabolism\", \"Flow modulated allometry\", \"Coral physiology and bleaching\", \"Coral-symbiont associations\", \"Network science and ecosystem resilience\"] AREAS_OF_INTEREST: [\"Marine ecology\", \"Biomechanics\", \"Oceanography\", \"Fisheries stock surveys\", \"Ocean acidification\", \"Global warming effects on coral reefs\", \"Underwater robotics\", \"Instrumentation development\"] BIOGRAPHY: Mark Patterson directs the Field Robotics Laboratory (FRL). He has spent two decades developing Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (AUVs) and free-swimming robots for marine research. His work has led to discoveries including coherent structures of lowered oxygen over coral reefs, krill swarm behavior in the Antarctic, and fish identification from sonar imagery. The lab holds patents in marine robotics (US 5,995,882) and machine learning for underwater imagery interpretation (US 7,221,621). The original Fetch AUV holds the record for longest continuously operating underwater vehicle. Patterson's research also focuses on the physical biology of invertebrates, plants