{"id": "lookup-konstantin-khrapko", "question": "What does Konstantin Khrapko research, and what is their title?", "stratum": "lookup", "kind": "prose", "ground_truth": "", "expected_slugs": ["konstantin-khrapko"], "source_facts": "NAME: Konstantin Khrapko TITLE: COLLEGE: cos SLUG: konstantin-khrapko RESEARCH_INTERESTS: [\"mtDNA mutations and their effects on cellular physiology, aging and disease\", \"Mitochondrial population dynamics and population genetics of intracellular mitochondria\", \"mtDNA epigenetics, such as mtDNA methylation\", \"Sources of mtDNA mutations, strand asymmetry and uneven distribution patterns of mutations along the mitochondrial genome\", \"Human evolution through ancient mtDNA sequences transferred to the nucleus\", \"Somatic mitochondrial DNA mutations and their abundance and relevance to human aging and disease\", \"Single molecule analysis of mtDNA\"] AREAS_OF_INTEREST: [\"mtDNA\", \"Mitochondria\", \"Somatic mutations\", \"Aging\", \"Carcinogenesis\", \"Mitochondrial population genetics\", \"Germ cells\", \"Early development\", \"mtDNA methylation\", \"Human evolution\", \"DNA fossils\", \"mtDNA pseudogenes\"] BIOGRAPHY: mtDNA Mitochondria are cellular organelles responsible for ATP production as well as many other cellular processes, from calcium homeostasis to apoptosis. Mitochondria are the only animal organelle that carries its own genome, mtDNA. mtDNA suffers high levels of somatic mutations which are suspected of being involved in aging and carcinogenesis. We are studying mutations in mtDNA and their effects on cellular physiology, aging and disease. We also use mtDNA mutations to trace mtDNA lineages and to study human evolution. PROJECTS: [\"Single molecule analysis of mtDNA\", \"High efficiency single molecule PCR supplemented with next generation sequencing (Illumina platform)\", \"Development of approaches for analysis of individual mtDNA molecules based on NanoPore and Pacific BioSciences sequencing technologies\"]", "notes": "cos; one entity, verifiable from the profile record"}
